From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rumisle <why-excuse-quail@duck.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 14:02:01 +0800
Subject: core/session: let plugins and API clients create child sessions

session.create accepts parentID (plugin API and HTTP), and session.fork
accepts child: true to make the copy a child of its source. Children get
the built-in subagent treatment: grouped under the parent, hidden from the
session list, and reachable through the parent's subagent navigation.

A child lives at its parent's location unless one is given explicitly, so
a client can pass both parentID and location and still get the right
location on servers that ignore parentID. An unknown parentID is a 404
instead of a 500. The fork flag follows the maintainer draft #51095
(Forked.child) so recorded events stay compatible if it lands.

Ocelot-Patch: core/child-sessions

